title: Essen and Hagen
subtitle: Two central councils give the Red Army different orders.
view-if: crisis_ruhr = 1 and e20_ruhr_council_done = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; e20_ruhr_council_done = 1
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= Essen and Hagen

The council in Hagen, run by the USPD, wants a settlement. The council in Essen, where our comrades sit with the syndicalists, wants to fight. Half the units at the front obey one, and half the other.

- @cadres: Send our old soldiers to take over the battalions.
- @unite: Merge the two councils under one executive.

@cadres
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. A better army, and an Essen army.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources -= 1;
Q.e20_ruhr_men += 6;
Q.red_guards_loyalty += 6;
Q.crisis_line_2 = 'Red Army: ' + Q.e20_ruhr_men + ',000 men';
!}

Party men who served at Verdun take over the battalions at Dinslaken and Hamm. The front stops leaking men.

@unite
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The towns will hold together. Hagen will have the louder voice.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.e20_ruhr_hagen = 1;
Q.e20_ruhr_towns += 2;
Q.uspd_relation += 4;
Q.crisis_line_1 = 'Towns held: ' + Q.e20_ruhr_towns;
!}

The two councils meet in Hagen and elect a single executive of nine. Three of them are ours.
